# Patch 1 (REQUIRED): /o capability lane through the single safe-link choke point
#
# Finding: BYPASS-1 / BYPASS-2 (A35, A36). buildCapabilities in
# src/fyd/object/view.ts interpolated raw contact values into hrefs with no
# safe-link gate: website "javascript:alert('A35')" rendered as a live
# <a href="javascript:alert('A35')">Website</a> on the /o object page, both
# directly and end-to-end through composeObjectView.
#
# Fix: route all three /o capability hrefs (call/email/website) through the
# existing resolveSafeLink choke point (src/fyd/sitespec/safe-link.ts: the
# single link authority; it imports nothing, so no cycle). No new
# SecurityAuthority, no second allowlist. An unsafe value emits NO
# capability (no fake buttons: the UI renders an action row from this list
# and nothing else). The /o contact block still shows the raw value as
# inert text (see o-contact-block-safe-link.patch). This also closes W2
# (A37): the "call" capability's TEL_ALLOWED rule rejects
# quote/attribute-breakout phones before any href is built.
#
# Behavior note: a website that is a bare hostname or relative path is now
# non-navigable (no Website button), matching the choke point's documented
# rule. Fail closed.
#
# Apply: git apply ~/workspace/fyd-factory/patches/o-capability-safe-link.patch
# (from repo root /home/nolan/projects/ping, branch fyd-factory)

